---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title={`Contact — ${site.name}`}
  description={`Email ${site.email}. No form, no calendar link — Ho Chi Minh City, UTC+7.`}
>
  <article class="shell page">
    <header class="page__head">
      <h1>Email. There is no form.</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        <a class="email" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
      </p>

      <p>
        I am in {site.location}, UTC+7.
      </p>

      <h2>What is useful to send</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A specific question about anything in the writeups. Disagreement about
          the statistics is more welcome than agreement about them.
        </li>
        <li>
          Work in Vietnamese market data, education technology, or LLM pipelines
          where the cost per call actually matters.
        </li>
        <li>
          Corrections. If a number on this site is wrong I would rather find out
          from you than not find out.
        </li>
      </ul>

      {site.links.length > 0 && (
        <>
          <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
          <ul>
            {site.links.map((l) => (
              <li><a href={l.href}>{l.label}</a>{l.note && <span class="muted"> — {l.note}</span>}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </>
      )}

      <h2>On code links</h2>
      <p>
        None of the writeups carries a code link, and the pages say so plainly
        rather than showing a link that goes nowhere. The quantitative work
        carries account configuration that has no business being published, the
        platform work is not my code to publish, and the extraction pipeline is
        a side project whose repository I have not published. If you need to see
        something specific from any of them, ask and I will tell you what I can show.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: var(--s-5) var(--s-7); }
  .page__head {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding-bottom: var(--s-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-6);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .page__head h1 { font-size: var(--step-4); line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .email {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-style: italic;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
</style>
